{:event/id #uuid "1544b41f-f905-4a58-b547-24bafd9d9c8d", :event/type :receipt-river/receipt-recorded, :event/recorded-at "2026-07-30T22:43:20.467Z", :event/schema {:id :eta-mu.receipt-river/receipt-recorded, :version 1}, :event/producer {:eta-mu/version "1.1.1", :package/name "@eta-mu/receipt-river", :package/version "0.1.0", :command "eta-mu receipt append"}, :event/subject {:repository/path "/home/err/spaces/eta-mu/.claude/worktrees/agent-operating-standard"}, :event/payload {:pi "eta-mu", :refs "none", :dod "receipt-river", :manifest "none", :note "Retracting the CLI findings in the preceding decision receipt. eta-mu on PATH is a volta shim to the PUBLISHED eta-mu@1.1.1 while the workspace source is also 1.1.1 with a DIFFERENT command surface: source registers top-level receipt/receipt-river/session/session-mycology/fork-tax in command-registry, the published build exposes them only under the git group. Answer to the question asked: YES, packages/eta-mu has the receipt subcommands. Verified on a correct build (pnpm -C packages/eta-mu build from the installed root, then node packages/eta-mu/dist-cli/index.cjs): help lists RECEIPT, RECEIPT-RIVER, SESSION, SESSION-MYCOLOGY, SESSIONS and top-level FORK-TAX, and receipt/session/fork-tax all run. RETRACTED: every create-subtask defect reported earlier. On a correct build create-subtask writes a semantic kebab-case uuid into kanban/tasks/ with type/category/parent/write-id/created_at and emits a kanban.task-created ledger event (2724 to 2725) carrying write-id, card-type and source-path. The stale binary did not error, it answered incorrectly. Residual real gaps: create-subtask omits labels/points/source; no root-card verb; leaf verbs are absent from the help tree, so receipt --help and receipt append --help render a self-referential stub and the usage strings are reachable only by typing a bogus subcommand; the published build also writes a degraded flat receipt with the package version in :pi instead of the event envelope; openhax.kanban.json now warns that JSON board config is deprecated in favour of openhax.kanban.edn. Also: building inside a worktree WITHOUT an installed dep tree exits 0 while emitting 163 undeclared-var warnings on await and producing a dist-cli whose receipt/session/fork-tax throw on an undefined await; the same build from the installed root emits zero warnings. Carded as link-local-eta-mu-cli-for-development, P0.", :ts "2026-07-30T22:43:20.467Z", :host "local", :kind :refutation, :origin "eta-mu", :repo "/home/err/spaces/eta-mu/.claude/worktrees/agent-operating-standard", :owner "receipt-river"}}
{:event/id #uuid "8de45e40-123b-4dec-a5a7-02b51d64d18a", :event/type :receipt-river/receipt-recorded, :event/recorded-at "2026-07-30T22:51:39.925Z", :event/schema {:id :eta-mu.receipt-river/receipt-recorded, :version 1}, :event/producer {:eta-mu/version "1.1.1", :package/name "@eta-mu/receipt-river", :package/version "0.1.0", :command "eta-mu receipt append"}, :event/subject {:repository/path "/home/err/spaces/eta-mu/.claude/worktrees/agent-operating-standard"}, :event/payload {:pi "eta-mu", :refs "none", :dod "receipt-river", :manifest "none", :note "CLI identity split per owner decision: eta-mu stays the published volta-shimmed build so other repos behave predictably; eta-mu-beta is the global entry point to this working tree. pnpm link --global on packages/eta-mu was attempted and reverted because /home/err/.volta/bin precedes /home/err/.local/share/pnpm on PATH, so the shim kept answering the bare name; a distinct binary name is the fix, not a PATH fight. Found and repaired a pre-existing dead eta-mu-beta symlink that pointed at /home/err/devel/orgs/open-hax/eta-mu/packages/coding-agent/dist/cli.js dated 2026-05-01, dangling since the workspace moved to /home/err/spaces/eta-mu; it now points at packages/eta-mu/dist-cli/index.cjs and works from any cwd. Second absolute-path integration broken by that move after the Rheos systemd unit. Verified: eta-mu has no top-level RECEIPT, eta-mu-beta lists RECEIPT, RECEIPT-RIVER, SESSION, SESSION-MYCOLOGY, SESSIONS and FORK-TAX and reads the board at 259 cards from the worktree. Documented in DEVELOPMENT.md under 'Running the CLI: eta-mu vs eta-mu-beta'; corrected AGENTS.md Board Operations, which had been instructing agents to run bare eta-mu kanban, i.e. the published build. Residual: eta-mu-beta version still reports 1.1.1, so identity still does not distinguish local from published.", :ts "2026-07-30T22:51:39.925Z", :host "local", :kind :observation, :origin "eta-mu", :repo "/home/err/spaces/eta-mu/.claude/worktrees/agent-operating-standard", :owner "receipt-river"}}
{:event/id #uuid "8cd6c0aa-c815-4b48-aab0-4ea6691f565a", :event/type :receipt-river/receipt-recorded, :event/recorded-at "2026-08-06T16:03:13.992Z", :event/schema {:id :eta-mu.receipt-river/receipt-recorded, :version 1}, :event/producer {:eta-mu/version "1.1.1", :package/name "@eta-mu/receipt-river", :package/version "0.1.0", :command "eta-mu receipt append"}, :event/subject {:repository/path "/home/err/spaces/eta-mu"}, :event/payload {:pi "eta-mu", :refs "none", :dod "receipt-river", :manifest "none", :note "PR-to-card binding sweep 2026-08-06. All 8 open PRs bound in both directions: PR bodies name their card uuid, cards in review name their PR, and the rheos-cli-card-lifecycle-authority epic carries the whole table. Two PRs had no card link: #158 (carries its own unmerged epic + 5 cards) and #176 (no card at all - created rheos-github-issue-projection through 'rheos create' so the board holds a task-created event). Merged #172, #176, #167. Fixed a confirmed path traversal in rheos card creation (--uuid reached the file name unvalidated; card-file-name keeps the last 8 chars so separators survived truncation and path/join escaped the card dir). Fixed a critical regression in #168 where load-task-or-fail passed the project map to load-tasks, readdir threw, collect-markdown-files swallowed it and returned [], so 'rheos move' exited 2 on every card while 98 tests passed. Roadmap survey found 3 false claims and corrected them visibly.", :ts "2026-08-06T16:03:13.992Z", :host "local", :kind :decision, :origin "eta-mu", :repo "/home/err/spaces/eta-mu", :owner "receipt-river"}}
{:event/id #uuid "3dac5466-51f8-4300-957c-ee4088a87904", :event/type :receipt-river/receipt-recorded, :event/recorded-at "2026-08-06T16:40:21.778Z", :event/schema {:id :eta-mu.receipt-river/receipt-recorded, :version 1}, :event/producer {:eta-mu/version "1.1.1", :package/name "@eta-mu/receipt-river", :package/version "0.1.0", :command "eta-mu receipt append"}, :event/subject {:repository/path "/home/err/spaces/eta-mu"}, :event/payload {:pi "eta-mu", :refs "none", :dod "receipt-river", :manifest "none", :note "Revived PR #158 (rheos EDN config) 2026-08-06 on request. Merged 74 commits of main. Four conflicts: config.cljs was the real reconciliation - main had :card-dirs support, #158 had projection escape validation, kept both; key reading stays kebab-only because parse-config-content normalizes EDN and JSON alike and both real callers reach resolve-configured-projects via load-config. Rewrote main's config-card-creation tests to feed raw JSON through the parser instead of hand-building camelCase maps that bypass normalization. Workflow was an add/add of two designs - took main's hardened job and folded in #158's permissions block, config-file path triggers, and a release-build step. Then closed all 3 CodeRabbit threads: moved normalize-config to shape.config (layering), closed a symlink escape in within-root? (path/resolve is lexical; confirmed the new test fails against the old check and passes against the new one), and scoped the file watcher to card-projection paths so notes quoting card frontmatter stop emitting false drift into the authoritative ledger. rheos 107 tests / 306 assertions, kondo 0/0, 4 release targets clean, built CLI loads the EDN board and warns on the JSON mirror.", :ts "2026-08-06T16:40:21.778Z", :host "local", :kind :decision, :origin "eta-mu", :repo "/home/err/spaces/eta-mu", :owner "receipt-river"}}
{:event/id #uuid "9b357463-f999-40e6-baff-e9048715116d", :event/type :receipt-river/receipt-recorded, :event/recorded-at "2026-08-06T19:05:19.774Z", :event/schema {:id :eta-mu.receipt-river/receipt-recorded, :version 1}, :event/producer {:eta-mu/version "1.1.1", :package/name "@eta-mu/receipt-river", :package/version "0.1.0", :command "eta-mu receipt append"}, :event/subject {:repository/path "/home/err/spaces/eta-mu"}, :event/payload {:pi "eta-mu", :refs "none", :dod "receipt-river", :manifest "none", :note "PR sweep 2026-08-06 second pass. All 5 open PRs verified bound to cards in both directions - no rebinding needed; no open GitHub issue matches any open PR, and the card-to-issue projector (#176) is merged but not yet run. Unblocked 3 PRs that main's advance had knocked into CONFLICTING: #169 (took the verb registry over main's hardcoded openhax-kanban help, after verifying the registry covers all 16 dispatched verbs; 110 tests/403 assertions, kondo 0/0), #158 (real reconciliation of load-tasks - #158 made a project map valid to carry :card-projection, #168 made it throw after it caused a silent [] and 'unknown task' for real cards; kept both by accepting map-or-string and throwing :usage on anything resolving no tasks-dir, and rewrote main's guard test to cover the same hazard under the new contract; 116 tests/329 assertions, kondo 0/0), #170 (ledger union - both sides confirmed pure appends, whole-line dedup kept all 214 new events, 2552+172+42=2766, nothing dropped). Fixed #157's real defect: its workspace-clean guard errored 'changed tracked files' but ran git status --porcelain, which counts untracked, and the same step downloads .review-context/ into the workspace - it tripped on its own artifact and never reached the model. Ignored the path and corrected the message. Roadmap second pass found 3 more stale claims, all describing in-flight state that expired on merge. Self-correction: a persistent shell cwd left a build and a board comment in the #170 worktree; reverted and redone in the primary tree - the '276 warnings / no node_modules' reading was that worktree, not the primary tree.", :ts "2026-08-06T19:05:19.774Z", :host "local", :kind :decision, :origin "eta-mu", :repo "/home/err/spaces/eta-mu", :owner "receipt-river"}}
{:event/id #uuid "6faaeb05-abc7-4ab5-b912-2a8f38e63de4", :event/type :receipt-river/receipt-recorded, :event/recorded-at "2026-08-06T19:36:30.049Z", :event/schema {:id :eta-mu.receipt-river/receipt-recorded, :version 1}, :event/producer {:eta-mu/version "1.1.1", :package/name "@eta-mu/receipt-river", :package/version "0.1.0", :command "eta-mu receipt append"}, :event/subject {:repository/path "/home/err/spaces/eta-mu"}, :event/payload {:pi "eta-mu", :refs "none", :dod "receipt-river", :manifest "none", :note "pnpm gates (scripts/ci-gates.bb) added and verified 2026-08-06 during the GitHub Actions critical outage (incident opened 15:22Z, still investigating at 18:46Z). Confirmed NOT a quota: repo is public so standard-runner minutes are unlimited; org open-hax is free plan, which only meters private repos. The script mirrors 9 CI gates from their workflow files, selects them by the same path filters the workflows use, and copies two assertions an exit code misses: '0 failures, 0 errors' in stdout, and WARNING-as-failure for sol/axxium. First real run found a FALSE failure caused by the local environment: stream-chat-no-provider-configured-test reads the ambient OPENAI_API_KEY, so with 35 provider vars exported the no-key guard never fires and fetch is called; env -u OPENAI_API_KEY gives 156 tests / 351 assertions, 0 failures on the same commit. The script now scrubs provider env to reproduce CI's empty environment and prints the removed names only, never values. Verified green: chore/board-close-merged-cards eta-mu-cljs + ts-packages in 40s; PR #169 worktree rheos + eta-mu-cljs in 70s. Carded the underlying test-isolation defect separately as the-no-api-key-test-passes-only-because-ci-s-environment-is-empty.", :ts "2026-08-06T19:36:30.049Z", :host "local", :kind :test-run, :origin "eta-mu", :repo "/home/err/spaces/eta-mu", :owner "receipt-river"}}
{:event/id #uuid "fd6415e0-1c52-4d89-923e-1f0a330f27dd", :event/type :receipt-river/receipt-recorded, :event/recorded-at "2026-08-06T20:15:11.286Z", :event/schema {:id :eta-mu.receipt-river/receipt-recorded, :version 1}, :event/producer {:eta-mu/version "1.1.1", :package/name "@eta-mu/receipt-river", :package/version "0.1.0", :command "eta-mu receipt append"}, :event/subject {:repository/path "/home/err/spaces/eta-mu"}, :event/payload {:pi "eta-mu", :refs "none", :dod "receipt-river", :manifest "none", :note "Local CI gates completed and all 4 open PRs verified green 2026-08-06, during the GitHub Actions outage. Full gate set 9/9 in 4m25s from the primary tree. Per-PR, running only the gates their paths select (what CI would have run): #158 feature/rheos-edn-config 6/6 in 215s; #169 docs/rheos-cli-reference 4/4 in 77s; #170 docs/agent-operating-standard 2/2 in 63s; #157 feat/opencode-mimo-review-agent 4/4 in 184s. Three classes of FALSE failure found and each fixed at the runner rather than papered over: (1) ambient provider env - OPENAI_API_KEY defeats the no-key test, now scrubbed; (2) biome descending into .claude/worktrees and refusing on nested root configs, so pnpm lint failed locally for anyone using the house worktree pattern - excluded in biome.json and .claude/worktrees added to the repo gitignore, which had only been covered by a personal global ignore; (3) a worktree with no node_modules failing the first step of every pnpm gate and reading as three code failures - now a preflight that exits 2 for setup, distinct from 1 for a real gate failure. Also corrected an earlier wrong claim of my own: the sol gate does not need ETA_MU_APP_ID/PRIVATE_KEY locally. Sol's deps.edn is the only one reaching outside the workspace, to private katamorph and event-ledger; CI mints a scoped app token because eta-mu is public and its default GITHUB_TOKEN cannot read sibling private repos, but a local git credential helper already can. Gate now checks git ls-remote on the dep repos instead, and sol runs green locally in 19s. Confirmed no Actions quota was hit: repo is public, so standard-runner minutes are unlimited.", :ts "2026-08-06T20:15:11.286Z", :host "local", :kind :test-run, :origin "eta-mu", :repo "/home/err/spaces/eta-mu", :owner "receipt-river"}}
{:event/id #uuid "fffdae9d-9416-435f-8cf6-f85b1adef34f", :event/type :receipt-river/receipt-recorded, :event/recorded-at "2026-08-06T20:33:49.835Z", :event/schema {:id :eta-mu.receipt-river/receipt-recorded, :version 1}, :event/producer {:eta-mu/version "1.1.1", :package/name "@eta-mu/receipt-river", :package/version "0.1.0", :command "eta-mu receipt append"}, :event/subject {:repository/path "/home/err/spaces/eta-mu"}, :event/payload {:pi "eta-mu", :refs "none", :dod "receipt-river", :manifest "none", :note "Closed all 11 unresolved CodeRabbit threads on PR #158, 2026-08-06. Three were real code defects, each reproduced by a failing test before any fix: (1) fs.stat follows symlinks and the recursive projection walk enforced no containment of its own, so a link inside a projected root loaded cards from outside the task root - test proved it, now lstat + skip links, which also removes the cyclic-symlink recursion that previously only terminated via swallowed ELOOP; (2) real-path fell back to the lexical candidate for any path not on disk, so a not-yet-created child under an escaping in-root symlink passed containment - now resolves the nearest existing ancestor and re-attaches the suffix, rethrowing non-ENOENT; (3) the watcher collapsed absent and explicit-empty projections with empty? while the loader distinguished them, so a board projecting nothing was watched entirely - only nil is unrestricted now, and the existing test was inverted rather than deleted. Plus absolute projection paths refused (portability, not escape - containment already caught real escapes), kanban/openhax.kanban.* added to the rheos workflow path filters, and one Setext-heading delimiter fixed after sweeping the other 6 matches and confirming all are legitimate frontmatter closers. Three design-doc findings all verified and amended: measured that --git-dir equals --git-common-dir in the MAIN worktree, which falsifies the design's structural-isolation claim exactly there; added base-commit scoping for pending events across a branch switch; scoped the checkout guarantee to application-managed paths. Two declined with reasons: the law.fsm layering point is correct but belongs to the existing eta-mu-quality-ratchet-layer-boundary-rheos card that ships the enforcement, and the receipts.edn:149 request would rewrite an append-only evidence entry - the same substantive point was fixed in the design doc instead. rheos 121 tests / 336 assertions, kondo 0/0, 6/6 local gates green.", :ts "2026-08-06T20:33:49.835Z", :host "local", :kind :decision, :origin "eta-mu", :repo "/home/err/spaces/eta-mu", :owner "receipt-river"}}
{:event/id #uuid "b6bea0fe-ff65-46f0-84b0-09626a56d0c0", :event/type :receipt-river/receipt-recorded, :event/recorded-at "2026-08-06T20:55:49.478Z", :event/schema {:id :eta-mu.receipt-river/receipt-recorded, :version 1}, :event/producer {:eta-mu/version "1.1.1", :package/name "@eta-mu/receipt-river", :package/version "0.1.0", :command "eta-mu receipt append"}, :event/subject {:repository/path "/home/err/spaces/eta-mu"}, :event/payload {:pi "eta-mu", :refs "none", :dod "receipt-river", :manifest "none", :note "Merged the rheos CLI lifecycle stack 2026-08-06 on local gate evidence during the GitHub Actions critical outage. #158 (14cd09d), #178 (2176ecd), #169 (7c6d8a3) all on main; order #167 -> #168 -> #158 -> #169 held. #169 could not merge through the API - GitHub tracks it as a stacked PR and both the merge and REST endpoints refuse - so it was merged with git and pushed to main after re-verifying gates on the merge result. Review was closed, not waived: 15 threads on #158 and 4 on #169, all resolved. Three real containment defects on #158 and three CLI contract defects on #169, each confirmed against code before fixing. Two findings declined with stated reasons: law.fsm layering belongs to the existing layer-boundary ratchet card, and CodeRabbit's request to strip #169's EDN docs was stale because #158 had already landed - following it would have documented a precedence the code does not implement. Also self-caught: the entry-kind helper I added on #158 emitted an :infer-warning that reached main because the rheos CI job never builds and rheos-github-sync ignores compiler warnings, unlike sol and axxium. Fixed in #178, local gate now checks build warnings, gap carded as rheos-ci-does-not-gate-build-warnings. Remaining open PRs: #170 and #157, both verified green locally, plus #177.", :ts "2026-08-06T20:55:49.478Z", :host "local", :kind :push-truth, :origin "eta-mu", :repo "/home/err/spaces/eta-mu", :owner "receipt-river"}}
{:event/id #uuid "fe79f2fe-555a-43f1-8de3-408968d5cd88", :event/type :receipt-river/receipt-recorded, :event/recorded-at "2026-08-06T21:22:16.287Z", :event/schema {:id :eta-mu.receipt-river/receipt-recorded, :version 1}, :event/producer {:eta-mu/version "1.1.1", :package/name "@eta-mu/receipt-river", :package/version "0.1.0", :command "eta-mu receipt append"}, :event/subject {:repository/path "/home/err/spaces/eta-mu"}, :event/payload {:pi "eta-mu", :refs "none", :dod "receipt-river", :manifest "none", :note "All five open PRs merged 2026-08-06 on local gate evidence during the GitHub Actions critical outage; the PR queue is now empty. #158 (14cd09d), #178 (2176ecd), #169 (7c6d8a3), #157, #170, #177. 44 review threads resolved across the five, none waived. Real defects fixed this round, each verified before acting: in my own gate runner, an unresolvable --base fell through to an empty change set and exited 0 having verified nothing (now exits 2), --audit promised path-filter drift detection it never performed and exited 0 after reporting drift (now compares pull_request.paths and exits 1 - it immediately found the rheos gate missing five paths CI watches), and the axxium gate omitted the JS-boundary ratchet. In #177's cards, the Actions runbook classified on step conclusions with != success, counting skipped and unset as failures, and queried only the five most recent runs. In #157, both docs required an OPENCODE_API_KEY secret the workflow no longer reads. Corrected CodeRabbit twice where it was wrong: its #169 request to strip EDN documentation was stale because #158 had landed, and its diagnosis of the nil/invalid drift verdicts as new-card races was wrong - none of the ten task-ids has a task-created event, and the timestamps cluster on git merges. That became a P1 card, then confirmed itself live: merging the last four PRs generated 78 drift events with no human action, 4 of them invalid. Three ledger merges resolved by true whole-line union with an explicit LOST=0 proof after discovering my earlier prefix-slicing assumption was invalid once a chronological sort had reordered a base.", :ts "2026-08-06T21:22:16.287Z", :host "local", :kind :push-truth, :origin "eta-mu", :repo "/home/err/spaces/eta-mu", :owner "receipt-river"}}
{:event/id #uuid "f7be0323-a93e-4f1c-943a-eb49d45f5899", :event/type :receipt-river/receipt-recorded, :event/recorded-at "2026-08-07T01:20:08.455Z", :event/schema {:id :eta-mu.receipt-river/receipt-recorded, :version 1}, :event/producer {:eta-mu/version "1.1.1", :package/name "@eta-mu/receipt-river", :package/version "0.1.0", :command "eta-mu receipt append"}, :event/subject {:repository/path "/home/err/spaces/eta-mu"}, :event/payload {:pi "eta-mu", :refs "none", :dod "receipt-river", :manifest "none", :note "Picked the P1 card git-delivered-cards-write-false-invalid-drift-verdicts-into-the-ledger off the board and found its own diagnosis was wrong. The false invalid drift verdicts are not a watcher/git race - extract-status in rheos watcher.cljs required a double-quoted YAML scalar, which only CLI-written cards carry. Plain-YAML cards (68 of 282 on this board) read back nil, and nil was published to the authoritative ledger as an FSM violation. Deterministic, no running service needed to reproduce. Second defect in the same three lines: the regexes scanned the whole file rather than the frontmatter block, so a quoted status in a card body was reported as that cards status. Fixed by parsing frontmatter with shape/content-parser and making status-verdict three-valued (unknown, not invalid, when unreadable). Proved the new tests catch it by restoring the pre-fix logic behind the same signatures and watching them fail. Found a second bug while working the card: eta-mu kanban comment --text recorded the literal string --text as the comment body and returned ok true, because the legacy translator bound text positionally while kanban help comment prints Rheos help documenting --text. Silent data loss in the sanctioned mechanism for updating a settled card. Fixed both spellings; blast radius was three probe comments this session, card file restored. Also caught: the FSM in_progress->review build gate runs pnpm test without scrubbing provider env vars unlike pnpm gates, so an exported OPENAI_API_KEY refuses the transition; and pnpm test rewrites the checked-in models.generated.ts from live network data. Both noted in the PR, not fixed. Evidence: 138 rheos tests/476 assertions green, clj-kondo 0 warnings both packages, 9/9 local gates. PR #182. Both trees left clean.", :ts "2026-08-07T01:20:08.455Z", :host "local", :kind :push-truth, :origin "eta-mu", :repo "/home/err/spaces/eta-mu", :owner "receipt-river"}}
{:event/id #uuid "cbcdda6f-f0a5-4a15-a684-de9df0fa9eb0", :event/type :receipt-river/receipt-recorded, :event/recorded-at "2026-08-07T02:28:38.522Z", :event/schema {:id :eta-mu.receipt-river/receipt-recorded, :version 1}, :event/producer {:eta-mu/version "1.1.1", :package/name "@eta-mu/receipt-river", :package/version "0.1.0", :command "eta-mu receipt append"}, :event/subject {:repository/path "/home/err/spaces/eta-mu"}, :event/payload {:pi "eta-mu", :refs "none", :dod "receipt-river", :manifest "none", :note "Walked the board and pulled kanban-cli-status-validation-bug (P2, ready lane) — the last card whose DoD was outstanding rather than blocked. The 2026-07-19 triage had already verified the rheos CLI cutover fixed the behaviour; what remained was that nothing HELD it. fsm_test covered invalid edges between two VALID states only, so a regression reintroducing a bogus target like in_review, or a write path that refused but wrote anyway, would have gone unnoticed until it corrupted the board a second time. Pinned the refusal at three layers: law (no state in either FSM reaches a status outside :states, valid-targets never offers one, a card already stranded on a bogus status can reach nothing), the single write path (move-task! returns ok false, card file byte-identical, no ledger event appended, nothing published), and the tool surface (kanban_update_status throws :kind :refused, the kind cli/exit-codes maps to exit 3, and writes nothing). Each refusal test paired with a legal-move test so a write path that simply never writes cannot pass by doing nothing. Proved the tests catch the original defect by bypassing the FSM verdict in move-task! and watching them fail exactly as the bug behaved — in_review written with a fresh write-id, event appended, ok true returned. Two things found while working the card, neither in scope, both real: the comment --text fix merged in PR #182 was NOT live because eta-mu-beta symlinks to packages/eta-mu/dist-cli which had not been rebuilt since the merge, so the first comment attempt again recorded the literal string --text and returned ok true — card repaired by hand, CLI rebuilt, binding verified; and the in_progress->review build gate ran pnpm test, which regenerated packages/legacy/ai/src/models.generated.ts from live network data (+2541 lines in a legacy package the TS deprecation policy says must not grow) — reverted, not mine. Evidence: 148 tests / 767 assertions green (was 138/476), clj-kondo 0 warnings, clean shadow-cljs build 0 compiler warnings, pnpm gates --base main 4/4 passed, FSM build gate green across 11 suites. PR #183, card in review. Primary tree carries only the ledger and the card I moved.", :ts "2026-08-07T02:28:38.522Z", :host "local", :kind :push-truth, :origin "eta-mu", :repo "/home/err/spaces/eta-mu", :owner "receipt-river"}}
{:pi "eta-mu", :tests "pnpm -C packages/clio run test:nbb; pnpm -C packages/clio run test:shadow; pnpm -C packages/clio exec clj-kondo --lint src test bin; bb packages/clio/scripts/lint_extern_boundary.bb", :refs "8a29a2b 660e396 0d505b3 d812fde 801991b", :dod "clio test:nbb + test:shadow 28 tests/60 assertions 0 failures; clj-kondo 0 errors 0 warnings; boundary lint clean; branch pushed; every top-level PR review comment has a reply", :manifest "none", :note "Resumed claude session 9b26ed61 on PR #280 (clio event-sourcing kernel) after rate limit. Completed the uncommitted schema-children generalization (8a29a2b) — including the half-finished lint_extern_boundary.bb scan-roots rename that left -main referencing a deleted var, plus .nbb shebang stripping. Then codex rounds: identity-conditional stale-lock rename closing the fresh-lock deletion race (660e396); runtime-independent numeric canonicalization via exact IEEE754 decomposition, pinned literals verified byte-identical under bb (JVM) and nbb (JS) (0d505b3); Malli :registry option values walked as schema positions (d812fde); pid-reuse lock hardening via /proc start-time comparison with kill(pid,0) fallback (801991b). Replied to all 7 previously unanswered top-level review threads with commit refs.", :ts "2026-08-09T10:42:13.683Z", :host "local", :kind :push-truth, :origin "eta-mu", :repo "/home/err/spaces/eta-mu", :owner "receipt-river"}
{:event/id #uuid "55fd5605-2c18-4926-b301-edff7f265016", :event/type :receipt-river/receipt-recorded, :event/recorded-at "2026-08-09T22:56:48.517Z", :event/schema {:id :eta-mu.receipt-river/receipt-recorded, :version 1}, :event/producer {:eta-mu/version "1.1.1", :package/name "@eta-mu/receipt-river", :package/version "0.1.0", :command "eta-mu receipt append"}, :event/subject {:repository/path "/home/err/spaces/eta-mu"}, :event/payload {:pi "eta-mu", :refs "none", :dod "receipt-river", :manifest "none", :note "PR #280 (clio event-sourcing kernel) review round: acknowledged then resolved the 6 remaining open codex threads, and closed 3 already-fixed-but-unresolved ones. Three commits. 11a3fad: schema reference discovery now follows Malli's own resolution — a local :registry's keys lexically shadow the catalog for the subtree they scope (so [:schema {:registry {:local/value :int}} :local/value] stops depending on a catalog :local/value); the full comparator family (:not= :> :>= :< :<=) joins the literal-position set; and :orn/:catn/:altn/:multi join :map as labeled-entry types. The orn finding as reported did not reproduce — labels were already skipped because element 0 of every vector is eaten as the type keyword — but the accidental correctness failed unsoundly in the inverse: [:orn [:enum :shared/value]] parsed as an :enum literal and dropped its real child, hiding a dependency. 6 new pinned tests, both directions. ab10d53: extern boundary lint reads parsed forms via edamame instead of raw text, so a docstring saying 'js/' no longer fails the mandatory lint; rules moved to scripts/clio/lint_extern_boundary.clj behind a bb.edn classpath so they are testable, 8 cases pinned in clio.lint-extern-boundary-test under test/run.bb. 030ba6a: npm allowlist ships bin, nbb.edn, and a new deps.edn recording malli/edamame/promesa for CLJS consumers; manifest exposes clio. Planned bin target was bin/clio.nbb and that was wrong — packed and installed outside the monorepo it failed with 'Could not find namespace: clio.extern.js.process', because npm links a bin as a symlink and nbb walks up from the unresolved script path for nbb.edn, and the env shebang picked a global nbb 1.3.204 over the declared 1.3.201. Target is now bin/clio.mjs, a launcher that hands nbb the real entrypoint and the package's own nbb while inheriting the caller's cwd. Evidence: bb 12 tests/30 assertions, NBB and Shadow CLJS 32 tests/66 assertions each, 0 failures, 0 compiler warnings; clj-kondo 0 errors 0 warnings over src test bin scripts; boundary lint clean; bb scripts/lint.bb --only clio --kondo-only and bb scripts/test.bb --only clio both green; published CLI verified running new/schema-root/append/canonicalize from an unpacked install outside the monorepo. Branch pushed to 030ba6a; primary tree clean.", :ts "2026-08-09T22:56:48.517Z", :host "local", :kind :push-truth, :origin "eta-mu", :repo "/home/err/spaces/eta-mu", :owner "receipt-river"}}
{:event/id #uuid "895ebb2a-15fc-40b2-b4d9-c65aff62652c", :event/type :receipt-river/receipt-recorded, :event/recorded-at "2026-08-09T23:19:22.783Z", :event/schema {:id :eta-mu.receipt-river/receipt-recorded, :version 1}, :event/producer {:eta-mu/version "1.1.1", :package/name "@eta-mu/receipt-river", :package/version "0.1.0", :command "eta-mu receipt append"}, :event/subject {:repository/path "/home/err/spaces/eta-mu"}, :event/payload {:pi "eta-mu", :refs "none", :dod "receipt-river", :manifest "none", :note "PR #280 round two: seven new findings from codex and CodeRabbit, all acknowledged with a plan, implemented, answered actual-vs-planned, and resolved. Five commits d7aebd1..ce1362f. 694619b: a Malli vector head naming a registered schema is a schema position ([:counter/amount {:min 0}] is that schema with properties applied); schema-children ate element 0 as the type keyword, so the dependency was invisible and an incompatible revision reported as compatible. Head now walked with the children's scope; no construct-keyword guard needed because catalog-tree rejects unqualified ids and every Malli construct keyword is unqualified. Two pinned tests including the shadowed-head case. 1ca5791: acquire-lock! opened with a+ which carries O_CREAT, so a misspelled or deleted ledger was created and appended to as a fresh empty history — the exact failure require-ledger-path! refuses on the read side. Now opens numeric O_APPEND|O_RDWR and append-event! checks by name first so the caller still sees :clio.ledger/missing-file. Same commit adds a locked-paths registry: a POSIX record lock dies when the process closes ANY descriptor for the file, so path-based read-text inside a critical section would drop the lock silently; read-text now refuses a locked path with :clio.fs/locked-path-read, hard-link limit documented. 18bccd3: boundary policy split host from rule — runtime-neutral .cljc with no IO, bb entrypoint keeps traversal and exit code, test is .cljc under all three runtimes; found a genuine host divergence in the process (JVM ReaderConditional is opaque, CLJS edamame yields a map-like value the map branch already reaches), now pinned on both. Pushed back on CodeRabbit's broader ask to move the runner to CLJS: every gate in this repo is Babashka and the file was .bb before this PR; CodeRabbit agreed the original finding was too broad. d7aebd1: both lock child processes use pnpm exec nbb instead of pnpm dlx nbb@1.3.201 now that nbb is a declared dependency. ce1362f: fcntl(F_SETLKW) no longer called a mandatory lock in README or source — it is advisory, mandatory locking is an unrelated dead POSIX feature. Notable: the new form-level boundary linter caught a real (is (thrown? js/Error ...)) in my own draft test on its first run. Evidence: bb 14 tests/38 assertions, NBB and Shadow CLJS 45 tests/93 assertions each (was 32/66), 0 failures, 0 compiler warnings; clj-kondo 0 errors 0 warnings over src test bin scripts; boundary lint clean; bb scripts/lint.bb --only clio --kondo-only and bb scripts/test.bb --only clio green; all 20 CI checks green on the prior push; published CLI re-verified from an unpacked install outside the monorepo including the missing-ledger refusal. Branch pushed to ce1362f; primary tree clean.", :ts "2026-08-09T23:19:22.783Z", :host "local", :kind :push-truth, :origin "eta-mu", :repo "/home/err/spaces/eta-mu", :owner "receipt-river"}}
{:event/id #uuid "d843fdef-1255-4140-9c97-1c997b044d03", :event/type :receipt-river/receipt-recorded, :event/recorded-at "2026-08-09T23:36:03.841Z", :event/schema {:id :eta-mu.receipt-river/receipt-recorded, :version 1}, :event/producer {:eta-mu/version "1.1.1", :package/name "@eta-mu/receipt-river", :package/version "0.1.0", :command "eta-mu receipt append"}, :event/subject {:repository/path "/home/err/spaces/eta-mu"}, :event/payload {:pi "eta-mu", :refs "none", :dod "receipt-river", :manifest "none", :note "PR #280 merged by riatzukiza at 23:24:33 (5dfa8e9) with all 20 CI checks green and zero unresolved threads; codex then posted two more findings ninety seconds later, so they were fixed as follow-up PR #282 against main (user chose that route when asked). 366e76d: append admission policy moved out of infra into clio.law.ledger/append-admission — AGENTS.md gives infra.* as transport with no domain policy, and the retry/id-collision/stream-slot decision inside append-event! was a restatement of README Laws 2 and 4 sitting next to the file descriptor. Verdict map with :admission/conflict naming the offender; infra keeps lock/read/parse/append and maps the verdict to the same :clio.ledger/* failures, error contract unchanged. Made the identity-before-slot ordering explicit and pinned it: an exact retry also claims its own [stream seq], so the other order reads a no-op as a conflict with itself — previously an accident of cond order. 337a140: boundary lint no longer descends into (quote x) payloads; the form-level rewrite had fixed comments and strings then walked quoted symbols as executable, so (def marker 'js/console) failed the mandatory lint. My plan claimed syntax-quote would stay scanned — that was WRONG and corrected on the thread: edamame expands syntax-quote into concat/list machinery whose leaves are ordinary (quote sym) forms, and disabling expansion makes edamame throw 'Syntax quote not allowed', so the distinction is unavailable. Documented as a known gap where the predicate lives and pinned by a test asserting current behavior, with the clj-kondo js* hook and clio's absence of macros as the mitigations. Also note: the CI job 'Review pull request with OpenCode MiMo' FAILED post-merge with 'couldn't find remote ref feat/clio-event-sourcing-kernel' — an artifact of branch deletion after merge, not a code failure. Evidence for #282: bb 22 tests/55 assertions, NBB and Shadow CLJS 53 tests/110 assertions each, 0 failures, 0 compiler warnings; clj-kondo 0 errors 0 warnings over src test bin scripts; boundary lint clean; bb scripts/lint.bb --only clio --kondo-only and bb scripts/test.bb --only clio green. Work done in a worktree at scratchpad/wt-clio; primary tree left clean on the merged branch.", :ts "2026-08-09T23:36:03.841Z", :host "local", :kind :push-truth, :origin "eta-mu", :repo "/home/err/spaces/eta-mu", :owner "receipt-river"}}
